                        <p class="itemintroduction">Here is today's CleanLaugh - &quot;City Preacher&quot;</p>
                        <p class="itemparagraph">Having grown up just outside New York City, I barely knew a cow from an ear of corn. Until, that is, I married a small-town Ohio girl. While I was in seminary school, I had a temporary assignment at a church in a rural community. The day of my first sermon, I tried very hard to fit in. Maybe too hard.</p>
                        <p class="itemparagraph">With my wife sitting in the first pew, I began my discourse: &quot;I never saw a cow until I met my wife.&quot;</p>
